My most recent game was the first one where I have gotten to the tower levels,
and I was hoping somebody would have answers to a couple of questions:

Implicit spoilers ahead


On the first tower level, how do you get into the inner rooms.  Once I got
past the drawbridge, and found the first secret door, I couldn't get into
the back rooms (ones with several dragons, etc.), except by the inelegant
expedient of polymorphing into a Xorn, then levitating over the various
traps.  I'm certain that there is a better way.

On the other tower levels, how do you get into the middle?  I searched the
entire boundary for secret doors using my stethoscope, but never got
anywhere with it.  I had to use the same trick as above to get in.

This trick, polymorphing into a Xorn, while effective, has certain 
disadvantages (very low hit points), which make it somewhat dangerous
to use in other situations.  After a related fashion, how do you turn
back into yourself after polymorphing into some strange monster (the only
way I've been able to do it is drop everything, then cancel myself).
In previous versions, you just hit @ when it asks you which monster
you want to turn into.  I'm stumped.

Finally, I have the same problem with the endgame that I had with the 
others, but in a much worse way (I hadn't really expected an endgame
level, so I had stopped on the first level, emptied out my wands of
wishing to get dilithium crystals (yes, I used the polymorph-a-pile
of wands trick extensively, including the cursed scrolls of genocide),
and had taken off most of my armor (I figured with my +7 gray dragon
scale mail, +7 katana named Snickersnee, and more than 2000 hit points,
I could handle anything I would run into during the rumored endgame.
Of course, I was wrong)).  I couldn't get into the middle; the
wall was too hard to dig through, and I couldn't find any secret doors
(and relatedly, I didn't know if I wanted to go through the middle
anyway, since I don't know what the objective of this final level 
